{# THE MONTH GRID EVERY CALENDAR IN THE PRODUCT IS DRAWN IN.

   THE PLATE'S AND THE CHART'S SIBLING: a module says what happened on which
   day and this is the whole picture around it — the stepper, the day heads,
   the cells, their fixed height, the day numbers and the "+N more".

   THE CELL IS ONE HEIGHT WHATEVER IT HOLDS, which is the rule the component
   exists to keep: a busy week must not make the month taller than a quiet
   one. What does not fit was counted into `hidden` by the builder, where the
   height is known — a module is never asked to guess it.

   A PILL'S COLOUR IS A ROLE THE MODULE NAMED and a paint the atlas chose.
   Filled means open, hollow means finished — the same reading the map plate
   uses, so a mark means one thing across the product.

   THE ONE SLOT: `controls`, drawn at the trailing end of the stepper row for
   the surface's own picker. It is the surface's OWN markup and is printed
   unescaped, so a caller renders it with Twig and never builds it out of
   anything somebody typed.

   Rendered by Twig\CalendarRuntime, never included by hand — a surface writes
   {{ atlas_calendar(feed, '2026-09') }}. #}
<div class="cal-plate">
    {% if title %}<span class="tab">{{ title }}</span>{% endif %}

    {# THE STEPPER: the same three controls on every month. An arrow with
       nowhere to go is drawn and not offered, so the row never changes
       width between months. #}
    <div class="cal-nav">
        {% if calendar.previousUrl %}<a class="mchip ghost" href="{{ calendar.previousUrl }}" aria-label="The month before {{ calendar.month.label }}">&lsaquo;</a>
        {% else %}<span class="mchip ghost" aria-hidden="true">&lsaquo;</span>{% endif %}
        <span class="mchip on">{{ calendar.month.label|lower }}</span>
        {% if calendar.nextUrl %}<a class="mchip ghost" href="{{ calendar.nextUrl }}" aria-label="The month after {{ calendar.month.label }}">&rsaquo;</a>
        {% else %}<span class="mchip ghost" aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span>{% endif %}

        {# AND WHAT THE SURFACE IS FILTERING BY, on the same line. A month is
           one row of chrome — the stepper, then the surface's own control
           pushed to the right of it — and a component that took no control
           left every caller to draw a second toolbar under the first. #}
        {% if controls %}<span class="sp"></span>{{ controls|raw }}{% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="cal"{% if gridStyle %} style="{{ gridStyle }}"{% endif %}
         {%- for name, value in attributes %} {{ name }}="{{ value }}"{% endfor %}>
        {% for weekday in weekdays %}<div class="dh">{{ weekday }}</div>{% endfor %}

        {% for cell in calendar.cells %}
            <div class="dc{{ cell.inMonth ? '' : ' out' }}{{ cell.isToday ? ' today' : '' }}">
                {% if cell.total > 0 %}<span class="dcount">{{ cell.total }}</span>{% endif %}
                <span class="dn">{{ cell.dayOfMonth }}</span>

                {% for pill in cell.pills %}
                    {% set hue = hues[pill.hue.value]|default(hues['subject']) %}
                    {% if pill.url %}
                        <a class="cal-mark{{ pill.closed ? ' done' : '' }}" href="{{ pill.url }}"
                           {%- if pill.title %} title="{{ pill.title }}"{% endif %}><i style="--pill-hue:{{ hue }}"></i><span class="l">{{ pill.label }}</span></a>
                    {% else %}
                        <span class="cal-mark{{ pill.closed ? ' done' : '' }}"
                              {%- if pill.title %} title="{{ pill.title }}"{% endif %}><i style="--pill-hue:{{ hue }}"></i><span class="l">{{ pill.label }}</span></span>
                    {% endif %}
                {% endfor %}

                {% if cell.hidden > 0 %}
                    {% if cell.url %}<a class="cal-more" href="{{ cell.url }}">+{{ cell.hidden }} more</a>
                    {% else %}<span class="cal-more">+{{ cell.hidden }} more</span>{% endif %}
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {% if empty %}
        {# AN EMPTY SEPTEMBER IS A FACT ABOUT SEPTEMBER. The grid is still
           drawn — a missing month is a broken page — and the sentence under
           it says why it is bare, in the house's own words. #}
        <p class="use">Nothing on this month yet &mdash; which is not a nought.</p>
    {% elseif caption %}
        <p class="use">{{ caption }}</p>
    {% endif %}
</div>
